ction stage. At this point, similarities between users are calculated on-the-fly, which can be resource-intensive in real-time. Item-based collaborative filtering concentrates the bulk of its computation during the training phase facilitating the prediction phase. It involves creating and sorting a comprehensive item-to-item similarity matrix. While this upfront computation is intensive, it facilitates a more straightforward prediction phase. However, despite the ease of prediction, the pre-computed similarity matrix requires careful memory management during the prediction phase, ensuring they can be stored and accessed efficiently to generate recommendations.
